cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "perezsky: Perez all-weather sky radiance distribution, plane irradiance and horizon masking"
abstract: >-
  Python implementation of the Perez (1993) all-weather sky as a radiance or luminance
  distribution on a discretised hemisphere, normalised to measured irradiance, with irradiance
  on arbitrarily oriented planes, masking by a local horizon with a terrain model, Perez (1990)
  luminous efficacy and export to Radiance. Validated against Radiance's gendaylit and rtrace.
authors:
  - family-names: Wild
    given-names: Michael
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7730-3064"
    affiliation: "ZHAW Zurich University of Applied Sciences"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/WildSolar/PerezSky"
keywords:
  - solar energy
  - sky model
  - Perez
  - diffuse irradiance
  - photovoltaics
  - daylighting
  - Radiance
